(Description)
Given an m x n matrix, return all elements of the matrix in spiral order.

--- Solution ---
class Solution {
    public List<Integer> spiralOrder(int[][] matrix) {
        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();

        int top = 0;
        int bottom = matrix.length - 1;
        int left = 0;
        int right = matrix[0].length - 1;

        while (top <= bottom && left <= right) {
            for (int col = left; col <= right; col++) {
                result.add(matrix[top][col]);
            }
            top++;

            for (int row = top; row <= bottom; row++) {
                result.add(matrix[row][right]);
            }
            right--;

            if (top <= bottom) {
                for (int col = right; col >= left; col--) {
                    result.add(matrix[bottom][col]);
                }
                bottom--;
            }

            if (left <= right) {
                for (int row = bottom; row >= top; row--) {
                    result.add(matrix[row][left]);
                }
                left++;
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}

--- Approach ---
- Four loop statements were solutions for this problem.
Because it should touch all elements to put them into the list, four loops made easier to reach them.

- Then, the question in here is how to reach them followed by the spiral order.
It set four boundaries, left, right, top, and bottom.
Those values roled as a base case in the outer while loop, if left value is bigger than right, or top value is lower than bottom, 
that means there is no more elements to touch, it quits the four inner for loops.

- Each four loops have their own direction.
From left to right, top to bottom, right to left, and bottom to top in order, and that was a spiral order.
Also, in last two loop statements, it checks whether the matrix still have elements left with if statment,
therefore it could safely add inner matrix elements as well. 
